# Git and Phase Workflow

## Branching

- Do not commit directly to `main`.
- Use phase-specific branches (for example `foundation/project-discovery`, `feature/phase-02-django-foundation`).
- Open pull requests for review; manual PR review is required before merge.

## Safety

- Do not force-push to `main`.
- Do not merge automatically without human review.
- Do not deploy to production without explicit written approval.
- Do not skip hooks unless explicitly requested by the repository owner for a documented emergency.

## Commits

- Prefer clear, purposeful commit messages focused on why.
- Keep secrets out of commits.
- Do not introduce application code before the phase that authorizes it.

## Phase gates

- Meet documented exit criteria and approval gates before starting the next phase.
- Discovery and governance documents remain the source of delivery control until superseded by approved updates.
